From 2476644c4c275b324b78f6b7066246df71362f04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HighAsCG Assembly <assembly@highascg.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:02:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ffmpeg/ogl: native DXV (Resolume DXV2/DXV3) GPU decode
 (WO-993)

Same shape as the NotchLC path (WO-820). The producer only undoes DXV's own compression
(dxv_unpack: LZF, stored, DXT1/DXT5 back-references, the DXV3 HQ opcode/FSE scheme; a port of
FFmpeg 8.0.1 dxv.c/lzf.c, bit-exact on every frame of 9 clips, ASan/UBSan differential fuzz
clean) and hands the filter graph a GRAY8 payload frame of raw BC blocks (core/frame/dxv.h).
The mixer uploads it and decodes BC1/BC3/BC4/BC5 per pixel in a fragment shader
(dxv_kernel.cpp) with texturedsp.c's integer maths.

- DXT1: identical to FFmpeg's decode.
- DXT5: the raw premultiplied colour (FFmpeg un-premultiplies; Caspar works premultiplied).
- DXV3 HQ (YCoCg, Y+A): converted to RGB (R=Y+Co-Cg, G=Y+Cg, B=Y-Co-Cg, full range). The CPU
  path hands Caspar raw YCoCg planes read as BT.709 YCbCr, i.e. wrong colours.
- <ffmpeg><producer><dxv-gpu>false or a user VF keeps FFmpeg's decoder.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MxpJi7ZHbr5bkwDuaHmchx
